s were two pistol events, free and rapid-fire; three rifle events, small-bore prone, small-bore three positions, and free rifle three positions; and two shotgun events, trap and skeet. A free rifle event had been on the Olympic Program in some form since 1896, with the exception of 1932-36, but this would be the last Olympics at which the event would be held. Usually shot over a 300-metre course (and at various times in the past at huge distances up to 800 metres and 1,000 yards), the event was the victim of an effort to shorten the distances of the Olympic shooting events, allowing smaller ranges to be constructed. All the events were conducted at the " [:a {:href "/venues/542"} "Hochbrück Shooting Range"] ". As in 1968, women were allowed to compete alongside men, as all events were mixed. Four women competed in 1972."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/51722"} "Rapid-Fire Pistol, 25 metres, Open"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "31 August –  1 September 1972"] "\n" [:td {} "62"] "\n" [:td {} "39"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/51723"} "Free Pistol, 50 metres, Open"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "27 August 1972"] "\n" [:td {} "59"] "\n" [:td {} "36"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/51729"} "Free Rifle, Three Positions, 300 metres, Open"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} " 2 September 1972"] "\n" [:td {} "33"] "\n" [:td {} "20"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/51725"} "Small-Bore Rifle, Three Positions, 50 metres, Open"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "30 August 1972"] "\n" [:td {} "69"] "\n" [:td {} "40"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/51724"} "Small-Bore Rifle, Prone, 50 metres, Open"]] "\n" [:td 